<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
I had a lot of fun last night and would like to send out a special thanks to Nef and Verser for all there help.  I really needed help in picking up the circle spells and getting the 'travel tooth' for CS.  Now I have to make it to level 44 fast so I can use Those other two spells.<P>Today I had some extra time before work so I went to the Great Divide and picked up that travel tooth.  (All by myself in a brand new zone.)  Woohoo!  Another money maker in the bag.<P>A note about my death and team play.  Last night while traveling I died and lost a yellow bubble of experience.  (The sad part was that it was to a greenie.)  Big deal.  It takes me a total of 50 minutes to make that back.  Death is part of the game.  Learn from it and move on.  Whining about it won't bring back your experince.<P>Group play.  The group last night was a lot of fun.  I've been playing solo for a while now and have to admit that I miss playing in groups.  However my laptop has a few words about it.  Well actually it's one word and that is "Ahhhhhhhhhh!!!"  Too much information.  Much like when I tried to play with the ash hornets in the Burning Woods.<BR>- I couldn't target the tooth, even though it was right in front of me.<BR>- Hard to follow or even autofollow.<BR>- Refresh rate of about 3 frames per second.<BR>- Even with spell effects off and server side filters and working on a T3.<P>The clipping plane is at it's lowest setting, sound and music are also turned down very low.  Sky texture is off etc.  <BR>Please keep in mind that this is a 700 MHZ PIII with 196 MB of ram.  Not too shabby of a machine but it all comes down to the graphics card and laptops bite the big one on this.<P>The good news is that I will be moving back toward more normal working hours pretty soon.  Perhaps then I can join in a little more of the group action.  Until then I'm going to try and level Leat as much as possible.  I'd like to drag him along on the next raid and perhaps help out in all forms of powerleveling others. . .and perhaps my next character on a different account.<P>Anyway, just some random thoughts and a few extra thanks.  Thank you, Thank you.
</FONT>
